<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  MultiModalKit — the privacy manifest (4x, AC-255, D-106 F-4 = A).

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. A consumer shipping this module to the App Store
  is asked what it collects and which required-reason APIs it uses. F-4
  was the fork: ship a manifest per module, or write a statement telling
  every caller what to declare. Ryad ruled A — "less work here, more work
  for every caller, forever" is what B costs.

  WHY IT DECLARES NOTHING. Not because declaring nothing is easy, but
  because it is what the source says. This library has no analytics, no
  crash reporter and no server of its own; audio, transcripts and replies
  are values in memory and in the caller's own storage. The only bytes
  that cross the network move downward: model weights.

  WHY THERE IS NO REQUIRED-REASON CATEGORY HERE. Apple's five common
  categories were searched for in Sources/ symbol by symbol — file
  timestamps, disk space, user defaults, system boot time and active
  keyboards — and none of them is used. A manifest claiming a reason the code does not use is as
  wrong as a missing one: it is an untrue statement filed with a store.
  That search is not a one-off. The symbol list lives in
  Tests/MultiModalKitTests/Diagnostics/PrivacyRules.swift, and
  PrivacyContractTests.swift checks it in BOTH directions on every run,
  PER MODULE: this target may not declare a category none of its own
  source calls, and its source may not call one without this file
  declaring it. (The pointer used to name NetworkSilenceTests.swift,
  which holds the network-silence proofs and nothing else — a wrong
  pointer that shipped inside every consumer's app bundle until 4x's
  review caught it.) (4x's review
  found the first version failing the second direction backwards — it
  demanded the API never be used at all, so declaring the category
  correctly still went red.)

  The whole argument, with the host list beside it: docs/HOSTS.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
